# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Secrets / key material — NEVER commit. The encrypted keystore lives in the OS
# app-data dir at runtime, but ignore any stray local copies + env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.json
# Android release signing: the .jks lives OUTSIDE any git tree
# (~/.signbit-keys/), and these point at it. Losing the keystore orphans every
# install permanently, so it is backed up in 1Password + offline, never here.
keystore.properties
play-upload.properties
key.properties
# Portable-mode keystore folder (next to the exe at runtime; may appear under target/ in dev).
data/

# Internal planning docs / notes — internal-eyes-only, NOT for the public repo.
# Only code + files devs need to compile go public; our own planning/notes stay local.
#
# 🚨 LLM_CONTEXT.md and docs/android-port.md are DEV-ONLY (user, 2026-09-03).
# They are TRACKED HERE ON PURPOSE — this repo is private and they are worth keeping — but they
# must NEVER reach the public repo. `scripts/build-public-branch.sh` deletes them when it builds
# the orphan commit; that script is the enforcement, not this file.
# ⚠️ They DID reach the public repo in the first push (2026-09-03) and the repo was deleted and
# recreated to remove them. The earlier reasoning ("an auditor should be able to read it") was
# wrong for these two specifically: the context doc carries §11 Roadmap and an adversarial
# analysis that together say what is NOT built and where the author thinks the soft spots are,
# and android-port.md is a plan for unbuilt work. Neither is an audit artifact.
# ✅ Public and should stay so: README, DEVELOPING.md, SECURITY.md, docs/vault-cache.md (written
# for publication, names nothing internal). The keystore/KDF reasoning is still a trust asset —
# it lives in SECURITY.md, which is written for outside readers.
# ⚠️ Before any public push, re-grep for the platform codename, the platform signer repo name,
# and internal doc names — new comments reintroduce them (this has now happened three times).
docs/*-plan.md
docs/*-notes.md
docs/internal/

# Local machine-specific Android dev overrides (AVD/Gradle paths off a full C:, etc.)
scripts/android-dev.local.ps1

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Staged portable builds (raw release exe copied out of target/) — never commit binaries.
dist-portable/
